+# Pickup reminders
+
+For volunteers proposing changes to pickup reminders, including switching to email to save SMS costs. Pickup
+reminders go by SMS because an email trial increased missed pickups and wasted fresh food. This page records the
+reason after volunteers repeatedly proposed the same switch.
+
+## Why SMS
+
+From April to June 2025, larder tried email pickup reminders. The provider reported that 34% of reminder emails
+were never opened, and missed pickups rose from 6% to 13% of pantry orders. Each missed pickup leaves a packed bag;
+its fresh food goes in the bin at closing time. The pantry lead reported that many members share one phone in the
+family and never check email, but do see SMS.
+
+Larder switched back to SMS on July 1, and missed pickups were back to 6% by August. In
+[issue 52](../../notes/issue-52.md), a volunteer proposed email again to avoid the reported €40 monthly SMS cost.
+The maintainer confirmed that SMS would stay: the saving did not justify repeating the missed pickups and food
+waste seen during the trial.
+
+## Sending reminders
+
+[The reminder implementation](../../larder/reminders.py) sends a member their pickup reminder the day before.
